<article class="env-lemma" id="081P">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/081P">Lemma <span data-tag="081P">38.11.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $U \subset S$ be open. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is locally of finite type and flat, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$U \subset S$ is retrocompact and scheme theoretically dense, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f|_{f^{-1}U} : f^{-1}U \to U$ is locally of finite presentation. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $f$ is of locally of finite presentation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The question is local on $X$ and $S$, hence we may assume $X$ and $S$ affine. Choose a closed immersion $i : X \to \mathbf{A}^ n_ S$ and apply Lemma <a href="/tag/081N" data-tag="081N">38.11.1</a> to $i_*\mathcal{O}_ X$. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>